<section class="welcome-row"><div><span class="eyebrow">APPLICATION DESIGN</span><h1>Project architecture</h1><p>Separated layers make the system easier to understand, maintain, and extend.</p></div></section>
<section class="panel architecture-panel">
  <div class="architecture-flow"><article><span class="arch-icon">◎</span><span class="eyebrow">PRESENTATION</span><h2>JSP + CSS + JS</h2><p>Accessible pages, forms, validation feedback, and responsive dashboard.</p></article><span class="arch-arrow">→</span><article><span class="arch-icon">⌘</span><span class="eyebrow">WEB LAYER</span><h2>Servlets + Filters</h2><p>Staff authentication, role authorization, HTTPS policy, and CSRF protection.</p></article><span class="arch-arrow">→</span><article><span class="arch-icon">◇</span><span class="eyebrow">BUSINESS LAYER</span><h2>Services + Models</h2><p>Input validation, domain models, and circulation rules.</p></article><span class="arch-arrow">→</span><article><span class="arch-icon">▤</span><span class="eyebrow">DATA LAYER</span><h2>DAO + JDBC</h2><p>Prepared statements, resource-safe queries, and transactional inventory updates.</p></article><span class="arch-arrow">→</span><article><span class="arch-icon">◉</span><span class="eyebrow">PERSISTENCE</span><h2>H2 / MySQL</h2><p>Embedded file database locally; managed MySQL with TLS for production.</p></article></div>
</section>
<section class="about-cards"><article class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">ISSUE FLOW</span><h2>Issue transaction</h2><p>Lock selected book row → verify stock and student limit → decrement availability → insert issue and due date → commit. Any failure rolls back the full transaction.</p></article><article class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">RETURN FLOW</span><h2>Return transaction</h2><p>Lock active issue → prevent a second return → calculate overdue days and fine → mark returned → restore availability → record return → commit.</p></article></section>
